          "These concerns deserve respect. Jesus is not soft: he overturned tables, confronted the powerful and told hard truths. A Christlike God is not a God without anger. He is angry at what destroys people, as a parent is angry at a disease. The relational reading does not delete the hard texts. It asks how they fit with the God revealed fully in Jesus. Readers differ on how to do that: some see progressive revelation, some (like Boyd) see God accommodating to his people’s limited view, others read wrath as God handing people over to the consequences they choose (Rom 1:24-28). These approaches are debated, and honest readers should say so."
