          "Romans 8:28 uses the verb <em>synergeō</em>, “to work together, to cooperate.” Many translations say “all things work together for good”; some early manuscripts read “God works all things together for good” for those who love him. Either way, the picture is cooperation, not mechanical control. The same verb describes the Lord “working with” the apostles (Mark 16:20) and believers as “working together” with God (2 Cor 6:1).",
